flowchart TD
  subgraph win["One browser window: React"]
    entry[index.js]
    vm[ViewManager]
    view[View component]
    layout[Layout and components]
    clients[Clients]
    vctrl[View controllers]
    rem[RendererEventManager]
  end
  be[Node back end]

  entry -->|renders| vm
  vm -->|picks by view param| view
  view -->|init singletons| clients
  view -->|renders| layout
  layout -->|data calls| clients
  layout -->|UI coordination| vctrl
  clients -->|direct send| rem
  vctrl -->|echoed events| rem
  rem -->|IPC| be

%% tip: index.js :: src/index.js — mounts ViewManager into #root.
%% tip: ViewManager :: Reads ?view= from the window URL and returns one view component.
%% tip: View component :: One of 14 *View.js files; ConsoleView is the big one.
%% tip: Layout and components :: src/layout/ — the React component tree (sidebar, content resources, popups).
%% tip: Clients :: src/clients/ — 21 singletons; the only path to data.
%% tip: View controllers :: src/controllers/ — 14 classes that coordinate UI state; never fetch data.
%% tip: RendererEventManager :: Wraps ipcRenderer; every event in this window goes through it.
%% tip: Node back end :: Electron main: controllers, LokiJS cache, servers.
%% tip: data calls :: e.g. JournalClient.getRecentIntentions(user, this, callback).
%% tip: UI coordination :: e.g. SidePanelViewController.showPanel(name).
%% tip: direct send :: Data requests go straight to a main-process controller.
%% tip: echoed events :: UI events go through main and are broadcast to every window.
%% tip: picks by view param :: ?view=console, ?view=fervie, ?view=status …
